// wdoc section: Terminals.
page wdoc_terminals { sites = [:reference]
  h1 "Terminals"

  p "`terminal` renders a monospace character grid as inline SVG, drawn with a bundled JetBrains Mono Nerd Font. The grid is populated three ways: authored text primitives, an inline ANSI-bearing `text` field, or replay of an `asciinema` recording."

  h2 "Authored text"

  p "`term_text` is the one base primitive — styled text placed at a 1-based `(row, col)` carrying fg/bg/bold/italic/underline. Higher-level helpers (`term_box`, `term_glyph`, `term_fill`, `term_border`) lower to runs of `term_text`, so the renderer only ever paints styled glyphs."

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
terminal {
  cols = 60  rows = 12  chrome = true
  term_box {
    row = 1  col = 1  width = 60  height = 12
    style = :rounded
  }
  term_text { row = 3  col = 4  fg = :cyan  bold = true  content = "Hello, terminal." }
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "Inline text"

  p "Set `text = \"...\"` and the bundled `avt` virtual terminal evaluates it (ANSI sequences included). Use this for quick demos of escape codes, cursor movement, and styling."

  h2 "asciinema replay"

  p "Set `source = \"rec.cast\"` for asciinema replay — frames are coalesced and replayed at the recording's pace (override with `speed`). Playback **stops at the end** (replay glyph in the chrome) unless `loop = true` is set."

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
terminal {
  cols = 80  rows = 24  chrome = true
  source = "examples/casts/demo.cast"
  loop   = true
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "Chrome & theming"

  p "`chrome = true` draws a title bar with a close `✕` on the right and (during replay) a play/pause/replay glyph on the left. A terminal's `class` list reaches the wrapping `<div>`, so a `class \"x\" { background = … color = … dark{…} light{…} }` themes the window. Default-coloured cells emit `currentColor`, so user themes flow through."

  callout "Bundled assets" {
    class = ["info"]
    body  = "The bundled JetBrains Mono woff2 files and the terminal-player.js are written into <out>/_wdoc/ only when a doc uses a terminal."
  }

  p "Next: [TUI Widgets](wdoc_tui)."
}
